values ('a5b6c7d8-9e0f-4a35-8c45-5d6e7f8a9b35', 'voice-and-movement', 'Voice and Movement', 'Voice and Movement introduces actors to the disciplined training of breath, sound, speech, alignment, release, movement vocabulary, gesture, and embodied character work. Students learn to make vocal and physical choices that are expressive, repeatable, healthy, and connected to text, partner, space, and ensemble. The course prepares students for Acting II, period/style work, production practicum, auditions, and rehearsal rooms where vocal clarity, physical presence, and collaborative responsibility are expected.');

