"description": "Students approach speech variation ethically and descriptively."}]}, {"id": "410404db-0ab5-4bcc-895c-73333ac62dd5", "type": "topic", "title": "Vocal Health", "description": "Actors need sustainable habits for rehearsal, performance, auditions, and recovery. This topic makes care part of craft.", "children": [{"id": "7e18a712-b457-43a5-807b-465bd16be614", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Daily Care", "children": [{"id": "b2adb536-d03c-4bc5-9904-9948281d00e0", "type": "concept", "title": "Hydration, sleep, warm-up, and cool-down"}, {"id": "37945ded-5c4b-4071-a78d-dabe4aa095e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Environmental irritants"}, {"id": "7a68653d-50c1-4fd7-9eea-a3e0bf18413c", "type": "concept", "title": "Recognizing fatigue"}], "description": "Students learn routines that maintain vocal readiness."}, {"id": "b891d417-4240-4760-95e2-6f3667ba650c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Load Management", "children": [{"id": "bdc50954-bbe3-4666-a58c-c65f05c3906f", "type": "concept", "title": "Long rehearsal days"}, {"id": "eb000fa3-0e49-43c8-8201-ecb6e89c6f13", "type": "concept", "title": "Shouting, whispering, and emotional scenes"}, {"id": "c9a4ad5b-927c-4a62-a316-088bd38d2625", "type": "concept", "title": "Amplification and room size"}], "description": "The unit connects vocal demand to rehearsal planning."}, {"id": "803d1933-c787-45a3-8668-d6153bf4f603", "type": "subtopic", "title": "When to Seek Help", "children": [{"id": "90a19851-9c43-4337-a20f-7da5a384be51", "type": "concept", "title": "Persistent hoarseness"}, {"id": "4cb897b5-9e94-4021-b1cd-2c8972bc36ec", "type": "concept", "title": "Pain, loss of range, and strain"}, {"id": "db31df65-c767-42d4-8840-c2287407629d", "type": "concept", "title": "Voice professionals and medical referral"}], "description": "Students learn limits of classroom technique."}]}, {"id": "355c0787-307f-42f7-87f6-180628bd18e7", "type": "topic", "title": "Body Awareness and Alignment", "description": "Alignment is dynamic organization, not a fixed pose. Students learn efficient body use that supports breath, voice, and action.", "children": [{"id": "92a586cb-5fbf-4461-8011-9e9006044811", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Body Mapping", "children": [{"id": "18fdc00d-bfc4-4a13-9f17-cc5eee22d324", "type": "concept", "title": "Spine, pelvis, feet, head-neck relationship"}, {"id": "bbd9dfd7-f32e-4756-aeed-9fe049940245", "type": "concept", "title": "Joint freedom and skeletal support"}, {"id": "67bcd57b-35bd-4acf-9b19-d17c67aaadd5", "type": "concept", "title": "Habit versus choice"}], "description": "Students develop anatomical awareness for performance."}, {"id": "3b662824-095d-42ab-980f-608d8a239dae", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Balance and Grounding", "children": [{"id": "aac5d7d5-2037-4391-852b-fc85927150f0", "type": "concept", "title": "Weight distribution"}, {"id": "b42f2d50-d591-4b82-971e-62ca9105b3cc", "type": "concept", "title": "Center, gravity, and floor contact"}, {"id": "7bf7566b-db3a-460a-b622-adc6d0a57254", "type": "concept", "title": "Readiness to move"}], "description": "The point is to feel available, stable, and mobile."}, {"id": "5787eb8e-c46d-4156-977f-797e55b00144", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Alignment in Action", "children": [{"id": "ca06b3aa-829b-4c88-aef6-adb50cdd2904", "type": "concept", "title": "Walking, turning, sitting, rising"}, {"id": "c68fde8e-8457-4f11-bf6b-3e5f214204a8", "type": "concept", "title": "Speaking while moving"}, {"id": "328fc1ec-c40b-4632-9bbf-d2b1388ce239", "type": "concept", "title": "Alignment under emotional stakes"}], "description": "Students carry alignment into rehearsal behavior."}]}, {"id": "62788324-ae24-41f6-bbb3-9be157e63973", "type": "topic", "title": "Physical Relaxation and Release", "description": "Release work removes unnecessary effort so actors can respond with precision. Relaxation here means active availability.", "children": [{"id": "abf0102f-53d9-47bc-97e7-df3eb79616b2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Tension Patterns", "children": 