inations"}, {"id": "5f2294b6-79f4-4f46-953b-a53f2dcfeeb2", "type": "concept", "title": "Character and relationship applications"}], "description": "Students explore how weight, time, space, and flow shape action."}, {"id": "119dcbd4-ab11-4339-ad38-05fd79810580", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Viewpoints", "children": [{"id": "1ef9bc12-aa18-4927-99b6-2c64ca570d6e", "type": "concept", "title": "Tempo, duration, repetition, kinesthetic response"}, {"id": "54852a67-7e5d-4cb5-8e75-d5f37f02f54f", "type": "concept", "title": "Shape, gesture, architecture, spatial relationship"}, {"id": "9575c81b-2b92-4f16-96e9-1e13fc7a9833", "type": "concept", "title": "Group composition"}], "description": "Students work with time and space as compositional tools."}, {"id": "8dfb9eb6-816c-40c4-bf00-c70f4a8c1ac4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Movement Scores", "children": [{"id": "443bb746-d702-48e6-9046-19ccdf02a3c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Physical sequence"}, {"id": "7e76e80a-0f7b-4675-b633-0ede16071772", "type": "concept", "title": "Cueing and transitions"}, {"id": "04695292-f0e1-4d1c-8bc5-aff7f48db989", "type": "concept", "title": "Notation and rehearsal notes"}], "description": "The unit turns exploration into repeatable performance structure."}]}, {"id": "aa83a022-5311-437f-8af9-586af1699e8d", "type": "topic", "title": "Gesture and Expression", "description": "Gesture reveals thought, relationship, status, and culture. Students learn to make physical expression specific rather than decorative.", "children": [{"id": "76671996-ef0f-4a57-986b-fba90228a747", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Everyday Gesture", "children": [{"id": "3f765fb3-b979-4095-aaec-5cd8b9f0085a", "type": "concept", "title": "Personal gestures"}, {"id": "c50930f7-1d2e-4b58-950d-9f5dd43188cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Social gestures"}, {"id": "05be5bcc-fb1e-42b6-95c5-0bf362428fa2", "type": "concept", "title": "Gesture and context"}], "description": "Actors observe how people communicate before words."}, {"id": "c6c17cb4-9052-465d-95fc-f52c721978de", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Expressive Gesture", "children": [{"id": "fa944338-b8f1-45ca-8b9e-a3b8e2a305f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Size, tempo, repetition, and focus"}, {"id": "1546a696-44a4-4d89-bec5-ca054eacf4c4", "type": "concept", "title": "Stillness as a gesture"}, {"id": "2e6a2113-7c14-435c-9ff1-f8e02229d01b", "type": "concept", "title": "Gesture in large and small spaces"}], "description": "Students shape gesture for theatrical clarity."}, {"id": "271a9762-28ad-402b-a246-dd56c75acde9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethics and Specificity", "children": [{"id": "fc855323-c5f8-483d-9490-4e2c29279e8c", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural gesture awareness"}, {"id": "08ce8bdd-858d-4aa1-b64f-d8aaa3d8ae93", "type": "concept", "title": "Embodied research"}, {"id": "d839840e-f882-4f90-a8ad-2b60c5041db2", "type": "concept", "title": "Representation and consent"}], "description": "The course avoids stereotype and shallow imitation."}]}, {"id": "19845050-d7df-4e8c-97e7-f2711720cffd", "type": "topic", "title": "Physical Characterization", "description": "Character lives through rhythm, posture, energy, and behavior. This unit links physical choices to given circumstances and objective.", "children": [{"id": "504ab915-7d62-4de3-9ebe-cfbc95296075", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Physical Given Circumstances", "children": [{"id": "c1239c35-3204-44d8-8070-e660b05f1eae", "type": "concept", "title": "Age, labor, class, health, status, environment"}, {"id": "ea8ab383-2f74-4b26-b7c7-c1b55f186183", "type": "concept", "title": "Costume and object influence"}, {"id": "bb437825-4ad9-400a-82f9-60a933d47709", "type": "concept", "title": "Backstory translated into action"}], "description": "Students ask how a character's world affects the body."}, {"id": "6890b997-d7fa-4a4b-831f-72ab4940e9c2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Rhythm and Tempo", "children": [{"id": "b3e5eed7-966e-41e6-b659-0a0f73eeabf2", "type": "concept", "title": "Walk, pause, acceleration, stillness"}, {"id": "1b6dc800-fb04-4908-ad4c-5a1510491135", "type": "concept", "title": "Private versus public body"}, {"id": "1126f76b-6aaa-4d59-8c6c-9846233ae1ac", "type": "concept", "title": "Energy shifts under pressure"}], "description": "The gist is to make character physically repeatable."}, {"id": "762894c0-00aa-4e51-9caa-7dfa8ea566a9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Transformation With Care", "children": [{"id": "04a6a8c1-6866-406a-9614-32bd4b7c69d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding caricature"}, {"id": "faa900e1-0299-486c-80f2-7148910cb676", "type": "concept", "title": "Access and disability awareness"}, {"id": "614f79fa-8731-47e9-bab8-1436766c464d", "type": "concept", "title": "Safe exits from character work"}], "description": "Students develop range while respecting real bodies and identities."}]}, {"id": "cb0fd3e5-4c46-4308-80e1-88b5eb657bb2", "type": "topic", "title": "Integrating Voice and Body", "description": "The actor's voice and body must act together. This culminating topic connects breath, speech, movement, text, partner, and space.", "children": [{"id": "cac25323-c632-4fc0-af24-ea83412e5a52", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Text in the Body", "children": [{"id": "2ccc2b5e-4eb9-4771-aa53-540d7e2485c6", "type": "concept", "title": "Operative words"}, {"id": "8feb050e-b00a-4b63-bf05-edd9a3e42724", "type": "concept", "title": "Breath, gesture, and thought"}, {"id": "d7acec25-e88a-4391-bfdc-b909e4fcc43e", "type": "concept", "title": "Verse and heightened text basics"}], "description": "Students physicalize language without illustrating every word."}, {"id": "3ba4046c-abf4-4455-a6d1-c79a992bec85", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Movement With Speech", "children": [{"id": "f1b66dbb-bd01-4f78-9d57-9594a833b467", "type": "concept", "title": "Projection in motion"}, {"id": "a6a573c6-3831-47f9-973b-4740d74efffa", "type": "concept", "title": "Pace, breath, and blocking"}, {"id": "7cfdeb90-f12d-4050-ae46-8ed330b6eb4e", "type": "concept", "title": "Action-driven movement"}], "description": "Actors practice clarity while moving through space."}, {"id": "51111738-62cc-41de-a0b6-23ae248ff3db", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Partner and Ensemble Integration", "children": [{"id": "af874f6c-3f92-4ad7-80b2-ade708e50473", "type": "concept", "title": "Listening through the body"}, {"id": "7b44e950-b0f4-4648-9212-ded23bfd30f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Group rhythm"}, {"id": "983d5c5d-11cc-4b98-a301-812f95c034f1", "type": "concept", "title": "Spatial relationship and cueing"}], "description": "The unit turns individual technique into shared performance."}]}, {"id": "454c390d-87a1-4de5-83ec-af3a195f607a", "type": "topic", "title": "Performance Sustainability and Consent", "description": "Voice/movement training must include safety, consent, and care. Students learn how boundaries support, rather than limit, artistic risk.", "children": [{"id": "34d99dd0-12cf-4400-91a4-bd7eaad3da78", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Consent in Physical Work", "children": [{"id": "079bd395-c02e-4067-a64d-867042916a8d", "type": "concept", "title": "Opt-in and opt-out processes"}, {"id": "54d0c9fc-3c73-480e-ab9a-92899387d25e", "type": "concept", "title": "Partner work agreements"}, {"id": "2db12c01-1514-4225-8c9e-945d404f6992", "type": "concept", "title": "Check-ins and repair"}], "description": "Students practice clear language around touch, proximity, and intensity."}, {"id": "915339c3-1241-43d3-a4da-8a05a89827f7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Nervous-System Awareness", "children": [{"id": "c5c70b53-ec50-488c-b7db-707c57a7f09d", "type": "concept", "title": "Activation and grounding"}, {"id": "d332e4f2-f9b3-4f96-a604-f82e48f5efbb", "type": "concept", "title": "Return-to-neutral practices"}, {"id": "f31eaa18-69b7-4082-bbd7-8c84bd7335b9", "type": "concept", "title": "Debriefing intense work"}], "description": "The course recognizes performance as embodied stress."}, {"id": "a298b6fd-6b69-411b-8188-de9d873af152", "type": "subtopi